{"name":"Dark and Stormy Night","hex":"#4f5a62","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"dark","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having an absolute or (more often) relative lack of light.","Extinguished."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A complete or (more often) partial absence of light.","Ignorance."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dark"},{"term":"and","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-3 language code for Ansus."]},{"part":"Conjunction","definitions":["As a coordinating conjunction; expressing two elements to be taken together or in addition to each other.","Yet; but."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/and"},{"term":"stormy","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of or pertaining to storms.","Characterized by, or proceeding from, a storm; subject to storms; agitated with strong winds and heavy rain."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/stormy"}],"entries":[{"title":"Dark and Stormy Night","blocks":[{"text":"Dark and Stormy Night is a 2009 independent film spoofing the haunted house and murder mystery films produced by Hollywood in the 1930s and 1940s. Larry Blamire directed and acted in the film and wrote the screenplay. The film also includes many cast members from Blamire's previous films."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/8/8d/Dark_and_Stormy_Night_%282009%29_Film_Poster.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dark_and_Stormy_Night","wikidata":"Q5223496"},{"title":"It was a dark and stormy night","blocks":[{"text":"\"It was a dark and stormy night\" is an often-mocked and parodied phrase considered to represent \"the archetypal example of a florid, melodramatic style of fiction writing\", also known as purple prose."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/de/Stormy_night_skies_in_Glacier_%284455539994%29.jpg/330px-Stormy_night_skies_in_Glacier_%284455539994%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/It_was_a_dark_and_stormy_night","wikidata":"Q647267"},{"title":"Night","blocks":[{"text":"Night, or nighttime, is the period of darkness when the Sun is below the horizon. Daylight illuminates one side of Earth, leaving the other in darkness. The opposite of nighttime is daytime. Earth's rotation causes the appearance of sunrise and sunset. Moonlight, airglow, starlight, and light pollution dimly illuminate night. The duration of day, night, and twilight varies depending on the time of year and the observer's latitude."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6d/Savault_Chapel_Under_Milky_Way_BLS.jpg/330px-Savault_Chapel_Under_Milky_Way_BLS.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Night","wikidata":"Q575"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/8/8d/Dark_and_Stormy_Night_%282009%29_Film_Poster.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 1x","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/8/8d/Dark_and_Stormy_Night_%282009%29_Film_Poster.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ADark_and_Stormy_Night_(2009)_Film_Poster.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/de/Stormy_night_skies_in_Glacier_%284455539994%29.jpg/500px-Stormy_night_skies_in_Glacier_%284455539994%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/de/Stormy_night_skies_in_Glacier_%284455539994%29.jpg/1280px-Stormy_night_skies_in_Glacier_%284455539994%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/de/Stor